         <change when="2025-01-06T19:15:03-05:00" who="http://papyri.info/editor/users/costasbala">Commit - The text in line 16 was mistyped in Greek  ι̣ν̣δ̣υ̣ξ̣τ̣ι̣ς̣ ηιεραξαπολ[λινε =&gt; ~|ịṇḍục̣ṭịs Hieracapol[line ][.?]|~la. I've also added some readings: line 8: α  ̣συνε  ̣  ̣  ̣  ̣  ̣ =&gt; ας̣ συνεδοκ  ̣. In line 23, where Rea had transcribed a zeta, suggesting a reading ἐπ]ι̣ζ̣η̣τ̣ε̣ῖ̣σ̣θ̣αι, the letter must be a beta when compared to the shape of beta in the subsequent βουλευταὶ: ]  ̣ζ̣  ̣  ̣  ̣  ̣  ̣  ̣αι =&gt; ]  ̣β̣  ̣  ̣  ̣  ̣  ̣αι. Finally, in line 29 the difficult form π̣ράσαντες =&gt; ἀ̣[γο]ράσαντες, i.e. bought (the wheat?) at a lower price, (prob. sold) at a higher price.   </change>
